WEBVTT

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:02.820
Thank you.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:45.450
Your ignorance makes me ill and angry.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:54.300
Nothing wrong with your television set.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:57.070
Do not attempt to adjust the picture.

00:00:57.070 --> 00:01:00.000
We are controlling transmission.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:06.050
control the horizontal. We will control the vertical. We can change the focus to a soft

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:12.490
blur or sharpen it to crystal clarity. For the next hour, sit quietly and we will control

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:18.440
all that you see and hear. You are about to participate in a great adventure. You are

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:25.890
about to experience the awe and mystery which reaches from the inner mind to the outer limits.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:08.060
mysterious gift is still evolving. What wonders or terrors does evolution hold in store for us in

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:26.840
the next 10,000 years? In a million? In six million? Mrs. Ives? Mrs. Ives? Perhaps the answer lies in this old house, in this old and misty valley.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:22.240
- What are you doing here? - I'm Cathy.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:30.000
I brought you a fresh bread and I was looking to be paid for it.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.920
by your housekeeper, Mrs. Ives.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.190
That woman is never around when she's needed.

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.090
It's impossible to find good help here.

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:39.010
I can't even find an assistant.

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:40.780
Fresh bread, did you say?

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:45.660
Keep it here.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:50.330
- One and tuppence, please. - Yes.

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.750
I didn't take any time out for breakfast.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:57.170
I've been working all night. One and tuppence.

00:03:57.190 --> 00:03:59.830
Thank you.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:06.360
- What kind of work is it you do here? - I'm a professor of genetics.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:09.880
This bread is very good. Do you have any more?

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:13.360
Oh, that was the last. But I can bring you some more if you can wait.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:19.360
I can wait. Only hurry. I can't wait very long for anything. Hurry up.

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:27.760
- Genetics? - Genetics.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.000
Ah, Darwin!

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:31.750
Oh, you're hungry, too, eh?

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:35.750
Well, you've had a hard night. There.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:40.640
- Have you teached him any tricks? - Oh, much more than that.

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:46.480
He earns his keep. Here, file these under M.G.

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:59.280
Molecular genetics.

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:26.050
- Why did he become so smart? - I made him that way.

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:29.670
- You do that with people, too. - That, my dear, is what I want.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:36.760
- Why do you ask? - I'd like to be smart.

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:47.990
- There's someone I'd like to be smart for. - Who are your parents?

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:52.920
I don't have any. Could you make me halfway smart?

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:06.300
- I'd like a sample of your blood. - Right, it won't hurt.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:19.270
- Extend your arm. - Yeah, I'll make a fist.

00:06:57.740 --> 00:07:00.000
at one a twopence, and all you bring

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:04.170
It's twelve and throppence. You're holding back one and nine.

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:07.170
- No, Gert. - Little Miss Innocent Eyes herself.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:10.330
Thieving from her own sister. Give it to me.

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:12.330
It must have been the professor giving the wrong change.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:16.330
I'm going to teach you to count if I have to beat it into you.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:19.330
No, Gert, I'll get the right change. I've got to go back anyway.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.330
- You want another blow? - Now, Miss Witch.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.330
Leave thy helpless child be.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.830
My customers cheat her out of the right change.

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:27.830
And she isn't bright enough to know.

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:30.000
Beating up. Never made anybody know.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:35.650
Right, Gert, that's love and fondness as makes ladies think the right way.

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:42.780
- Now, you know that, don't you, Gert? - Please, Wilt. Please, Wilt.

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:45.540
I'll let you go if you'll give me one little sisterly kiss.

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:48.460
- Hey, knock it off, Wilt. - Hey, distract me, friend, Gert.

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:51.280
He annoys me terrible.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:54.480
Ain't this town dirty enough?

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:07.110
- Thanks, Willem. - Well, if the professor wants another loss, take it to him.

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:14.530
I'm going that way. I'll walk with you.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:26.590
The foreman told the manager that I've been making trouble among the miners.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.760
Spreading discontent.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.640
and acting myself superior.

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:37.260
The manager called me in his office,

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:40.650
asked me if I thought I was too good for the job.

00:08:40.650 --> 00:08:43.370
So I told him, as maybe I was.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:48.050
So it's down tools for me, and I'm out of a job.

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:53.000
- Well, that's it, isn't it? - Yes, Willem.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.560
All right, then, I'll wait for you here.

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:59.420
No, come on.

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:00.000
Well, there's one going on.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.340
I'll be able to turn my back on that mine.

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:05.740
I wish I could turn my back on that whole town forever.

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:09.650
Life should go forward, see, and not backward like here.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:11.730
How can a man go forward here?

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:13.730
It's the most backward place in the world.

00:09:13.730 --> 00:09:17.510
- Where would you go, then? - Oh, anywhere.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:21.430
To get out from under, away from all this dirt and stupidity,

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:24.740
and away from that black mine that's to blame for it all.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:35.120
It would give me great pleasure to see this whole town utterly destroyed.

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:39.220
You'll go forward, Gwilym. You're smarter than the others.

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:42.420
Well, I'm too smart to go on eating coal dust for the rest of my life.

00:09:42.420 --> 00:09:45.080
I wish I was smart.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:49.010
Well, you're not stupid. There's a big difference between you and them others.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:52.570
All I need is one lucky break, see?

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:56.000
A job where I could use my head and I'd show them.

00:09:56.020 --> 00:10:00.000
I'd be riding around in a sports car and wearing a big gold suit.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:12.990
- Put a ring on my finger.

00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:14.470
So that's him.

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:16.260
- Who?

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:17.370
- I said from London.

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:20.540
- Oh, why don't you ask him for a job?

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:22.920
- Don't be ridiculous.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:54.960
Excuse me, Professor Mathers. Young Cathy's come to see you.

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:57.650
Oh, Cathy, show her in, Mrs. Ives.

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:07.270
I'm sorry I have to disappoint you. I'm afraid your blood is the wrong type.

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:12.760
Professor, it wasn't for that I'd come. Here's my friend, Willem Griffith.

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:25.340
Cathy here tells me you're in need of an assistant. I come to apply for the job.

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:30.000
Do you think you're eligible?

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:35.000
- For this particular job? - Can do anything another man can do.

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:36.820
And better, maybe.

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:44.630
I'm working on high-frequency electronics on a molecular level.

00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:47.960
Are you familiar with solid-state circuitry?

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:50.740
Any experience in ordinary lab techniques?

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:54.900
Microscopy, biopsy, protein analysis and synthesis.

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:58.420
Know anything about the mechanical side of office work?

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:00.000
Computer technology?

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:03.230
Filing procedures? Stenography?

00:12:03.390 --> 00:12:05.020
Are you trying to make a fool of me?

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:06.210
On the contrary.

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:11.150
It's merely suggesting that you are best adapted for what you've been doing.

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:14.650
Wait. If you could teach that monkey,

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:17.730
couldn't you teach Gwilym, who's smarter than anyone else in town?

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:20.550
I'm afraid it isn't that simple.

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:25.930
Learning is worthless without the brain capacity to use it.

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:30.000
That's what I'm working on, racing against time, trying to save...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.260
speed up the slow process of evolution

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:34.380
by a molecular approach to genetics.

00:12:35.740 --> 00:12:37.280
I've already succeeded with that ape.

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:39.210
He's almost human.

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:53.680
Now, if I could do it with a man,

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:56.660
if I could create the man of the future,

00:12:56.660 --> 00:13:00.000
he could rise above the animal passion.

00:13:00.380 --> 00:13:03.510
which lead to violence and self-destruction,

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:06.270
and develop the intelligence that's necessary

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:10.240
for a peaceful and civilized coexistence.

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:16.480
- Will you do it with me? - You?

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:26.340
Yes.

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:33.040
Realize an experiment always has its dangers.

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:35.960
I'm game for anything.

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:39.340
Sooner than go crawling back to that mine after my job.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:42.460
Spend the best of my life like an animal in the dark.

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:48.510
Mrs. Ives!

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:56.310
Pick him out and clean him up, Mrs. Ives.

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:32.950
Would you take your jacket off and sit down over there?

00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:50.160
Take a sample of your blood and stand your arm.

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:58.920
When the physical test is completed, and if it's successful, well...

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:20.350
- Take a fist.

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:24.830
- I passed the test.

00:15:24.830 --> 00:15:26.750
- Get on with it then.

00:15:26.750 --> 00:15:27.610
- Immediately.

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:30.000
- What do we do then?

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:35.990
The use of selective wavelengths can stimulate the genes in every cell of your body

00:15:36.090 --> 00:15:40.270
so that the superior genes become much stronger than the backward ones

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:42.090
and eventually dominate them.

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:47.800
Hereby accelerating the inborn mechanism of evolution to a fantastically high speed.

00:15:47.900 --> 00:15:53.370
These generators are directed into this chamber.

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:56.210
They are controlled by this panel.

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:21.920
This lever encompasses the entire evolutionary history of the human race.

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:25.570
Backward to the protozoa, forward

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:34.800
Each degree on this dial represents 10,000 years of evolution per minute.

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:38.710
You'll be the first man ever to go forward into our biological future.

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:42.290
You're still determined to go through with it?

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:47.570
That your experiment may be a blessing and not a curse on mankind.

00:19:14.970 --> 00:19:19.040
Now you're hoping you may be forgiven for what you did only a few years ago.

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:24.770
You helped to invent an atomic bomb that was so powerful it could destroy all the life.

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:43.030
It's this sense of guilt that's made you bury yourself down here,

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:48.720
trying desperately to find a way of making war impossible.

00:19:53.280 --> 00:19:54.290
How do you know that?

00:20:11.550 --> 00:20:16.550
- It's your dinner tray. To you and the young man. - Leave it, Mrs. Ives.

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:20.230
- We can't be disturbed now. - As you like, sir.

00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:38.440
- Don't let it get cold now, sir. - All right. Good night, Mrs. Ives.

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:43.540
It's very unwise and premature for me to see you at this stage.

00:20:44.020 --> 00:20:46.040
You didn't tell me my body would change.

00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:50.920
I wasn't prepared for a physical mutation in the man of 20,000 years from now.

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:56.630
Well, that's understandable, since we evolved from the caveman in Lest High.

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:10.880
- Why didn't he change? - Not all species of monkey evolved into man.

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:13.280
His obviously lacked that potential.

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:20.440
Your heightened forehead indicates more currents in your neuronic synapses...

00:21:20.520 --> 00:21:23.360
required for greater intelligence and telepathic function.

00:21:25.070 --> 00:21:30.000
Your eyes have developed a wider field of vision and a power of charge...

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:34.480
A charge of concentration.

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:37.530
Your hand reveals the bud of a sixth finger,

00:21:37.530 --> 00:21:44.630
which suggests an additional dexterity will develop in the man of the dim future.

00:21:44.630 --> 00:21:49.460
It is a high price to pay for power over other men.

00:21:49.460 --> 00:21:58.420
Misgivings, Professor.

00:22:08.730 --> 00:22:11.130
Afraid you maybe gave power to the wrong man?

00:22:13.910 --> 00:22:17.340
What makes you say that?

00:22:18.810 --> 00:22:24.870
You should have realized by now, Professor Mathers, that I can read your mind.

00:22:50.700 --> 00:22:54.940
- Professor? - Yes, what is it?

00:22:55.100 --> 00:22:59.640
Are you all right? You've not touched your dinner tree. It's stood here all night.

00:23:01.500 --> 00:23:04.880
- Come away, Mrs. Ives. - Very good, sir.

00:23:04.960 --> 00:23:29.280
Useless like the others.

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:34.560
An intelligence test is unsufficiently developed to measure your mind in its advanced state.

00:23:34.660 --> 00:23:36.660
What good is intelligence without knowledge?

00:23:36.690 --> 00:23:41.330
Hungry to know things, to learn everything.

00:23:45.200 --> 00:23:49.080
Catch me books.

00:23:49.130 --> 00:23:50.840
Books about everything.

00:23:50.940 --> 00:23:52.360
All the books you have.

00:23:52.460 --> 00:23:54.640
I want to read them all. Do you understand?

00:24:01.440 --> 00:24:07.730
- Two loaves, two insopence. Here you are, love. - Thank you, Mrs. Ives.

00:24:08.020 --> 00:24:10.690
Uh, how is Willem keeping himself?

00:24:10.750 --> 00:24:13.280
I ain't seen hide the hair of him since he first come.

00:24:13.490 --> 00:24:16.550
Something peculiar is going on, and that can't be good.

00:24:16.780 --> 00:24:20.100
Look what the professor done with that monkey. It ain't natural.

00:24:20.340 --> 00:24:23.390
- If you was to tell Willem... - That won't do no good.

00:24:23.890 --> 00:24:26.180
One of these days, I'll get to the bottom of it.

00:24:26.390 --> 00:24:30.000
- Maybe he'd seen me. Please. - If you don't believe me...

00:24:51.440 --> 00:24:52.220
have a visitor.

00:24:54.220 --> 00:24:56.500
I can't see anyone.

00:24:57.400 --> 00:24:58.300
It's me.

00:24:59.300 --> 00:25:00.000
It's Miss Kathy.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:02.150
Where has he come to see you?

00:25:02.150 --> 00:25:07.410
Get away! Don't bother me.

00:25:07.410 --> 00:25:08.320
That's right, he is.

00:25:08.320 --> 00:25:13.570
Not wanting the likes of me breaking in on his studies.

00:26:16.320 --> 00:26:18.320
It's been years since I heard your tender voice.

00:26:18.520 --> 00:26:21.710
Don't be daft. What have I got to sing about?

00:26:21.890 --> 00:26:27.080
It's a funeral dirge I'd be for all the last things.

00:26:30.030 --> 00:26:33.080
Speaking of lost things, where have you been?

00:26:33.080 --> 00:26:34.490
Delivering the breadgurt.

00:26:34.490 --> 00:26:37.510
All this time?

00:26:37.510 --> 00:26:40.510
What do you do with such a plain-faced liar, eh?

00:26:40.510 --> 00:26:41.720
Plain-faced?

00:26:41.720 --> 00:26:43.720
Oh, I don't say plain-faced.

00:26:43.720 --> 00:26:47.770
I say, um, fitchy.

00:26:47.770 --> 00:26:49.200
Aye.

00:26:49.200 --> 00:26:51.050
Maybe even pretty.

00:26:51.050 --> 00:26:53.540
In a sad way.

00:26:53.540 --> 00:26:59.630
Get a move on.

00:26:59.630 --> 00:27:00.000
Speak to it.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:05.690
gentle girl. She's hurting enough these days. That's true, ain't it?

00:27:05.760 --> 00:27:06.600
Please, Wilt.

00:27:06.910 --> 00:27:10.500
Not seeing handsome hide and her golden hair, your precious Willem.

00:27:10.500 --> 00:27:13.280
Thou must be hurting you real deep.

00:27:13.350 --> 00:27:16.620
Oh, leave her be, Wilt. He isn't a precious anything.

00:27:16.640 --> 00:27:22.820
He's busy. He's very busy doing very important work and trying to better himself.

00:27:22.840 --> 00:27:25.600
Trying to make himself better than any of us will ever be.

00:27:26.020 --> 00:27:29.850
How is that typical?

00:27:30.350 --> 00:27:33.940
The little thing finally speaks her peace, and who does she speak it for?

00:27:34.150 --> 00:27:38.260
Our worthless rotterers can't even hold down a job in an honourable profession.

00:27:38.340 --> 00:27:41.970
You can laugh at me, but you can't laugh at him. He's not to be laughed at.

00:29:13.920 --> 00:29:27.970
Professor, you've given me the ability to observe your culture through the eyes of a man 20,000 years in the future.

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:34.720
It's amazing, isn't it? Things that endure the ravages of time and taste.

00:29:35.380 --> 00:29:37.530
This simple prelude, for instance.

00:29:38.160 --> 00:29:45.620
Mark will quite probably outlive us all.

00:29:46.180 --> 00:29:48.080
Have you always been able to play this well?

00:29:48.180 --> 00:29:52.520
I have never before touched the keys of a piano.

00:29:52.740 --> 00:29:56.900
But playing the piano is only a matter of mathematics,

00:29:57.000 --> 00:29:59.160
and to a certain degree of manual dexterity.

00:30:02.810 --> 00:30:11.550
- Man produces little that is lasting, truly lasting.

00:30:11.550 --> 00:30:12.710
It's understandable.

00:30:18.540 --> 00:30:25.580
Fear, informity, immorality, these are heavy burdens,

00:30:25.580 --> 00:30:27.340
great drainers of creative energy.

00:30:27.340 --> 00:30:29.050
And when we are drained of creative energy,

00:30:29.050 --> 00:30:30.000
we do not create.

00:30:32.010 --> 00:30:52.370
- Procreate. You must get some sleep. - Yes, you must.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:01.120
Paying won't disturb me.

00:31:05.650 --> 00:31:07.030
I shall stop soon, anyway.

00:31:11.930 --> 00:31:15.540
Good night, then.

00:31:18.040 --> 00:31:18.820
Good night, Professor.

00:31:50.320 --> 00:31:51.460
I finished these books.

00:31:55.570 --> 00:31:56.720
It was dawn.

00:31:57.120 --> 00:31:58.520
Why aren't you asleep?

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:01.740
I no longer have any need for sleep.

00:32:08.180 --> 00:32:11.820
It continued to evolve.

00:32:13.040 --> 00:32:15.320
Your hand, the sixth finger.

00:32:18.210 --> 00:32:19.270
When did it develop?

00:32:20.520 --> 00:32:21.630
Sometime during the night.

00:32:22.390 --> 00:32:24.290
I was too absorbed in reading to notice it.

00:32:25.190 --> 00:32:26.010
How is it possible?

00:32:26.730 --> 00:32:28.510
Must the pupil explain to the teacher?

00:32:29.380 --> 00:32:30.000
It's really quite simple.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:35.050
It's quite simple. You released the mechanism of evolution, which is a self-generating force.

00:32:35.050 --> 00:32:38.190
It is now mutating under its own impetus.

00:32:38.190 --> 00:32:43.920
I am now where man will be approximately one million years from today.

00:32:43.920 --> 00:32:47.580
Why are you laughing?

00:32:47.580 --> 00:32:50.250
I am laughing at what is in your mind, Professor.

00:32:50.250 --> 00:32:52.180
You think that I've become a monster.

00:32:52.180 --> 00:32:55.100
Did I remind you that everything is relative?

00:32:55.100 --> 00:32:58.390
To me, you look as monstrous as the missing link.

00:33:02.650 --> 00:33:06.360
We'll stop this self-generating process before it's too late.

00:33:06.780 --> 00:33:08.580
We must return to the chamber immediately.

00:33:08.680 --> 00:33:13.280
I'll set the dial backward somewhere nearer to man.

00:33:15.920 --> 00:33:23.650
Would you be willing to go back to an ape, Professor?

00:33:36.460 --> 00:33:40.110
- More books for you? - Outside.

00:33:40.360 --> 00:33:41.400
Very good, sir.

00:34:01.080 --> 00:34:05.430
Wait, no, please.

00:34:15.240 --> 00:34:30.000
She's dead.

00:34:34.540 --> 00:34:42.460
- An accident? - Your race is too prejudiced to tolerate any differences from its own kind.

00:34:42.460 --> 00:34:47.300
She saw me only as a monster, and it was in her mind to run to the village and arouse its inhabitants.

00:34:47.300 --> 00:34:51.070
They would come with their primitive weapons to obliterate me.

00:34:51.070 --> 00:34:58.920
- I wanted to stop her, and I stopped her heart. - You feel no remorse?

00:35:00.990 --> 00:35:08.390
- What would it bring her back? - She was, after all, a human being.

00:35:09.460 --> 00:35:14.050
- The same as ourselves. - The same as you, Professor.

00:35:15.690 --> 00:35:20.490
In relation to me, she was no more advanced than a monkey.

00:35:21.200 --> 00:35:24.100
She wouldn't have become civilized for another million years.

00:36:08.480 --> 00:36:10.980
She was strong as an ox.

00:36:10.980 --> 00:36:13.220
That woman's heart stopped.

00:36:13.220 --> 00:36:21.670
'Cause somebody put the fear or the devil in her griffith.

00:36:30.730 --> 00:36:33.660
are going on up there. It's going to get to the bottom

00:36:33.660 --> 00:36:36.540
of it. Look at her now.

00:36:38.090 --> 00:36:45.030
Poor soul. Telling all

00:36:45.030 --> 00:36:47.480
of this to you, Constable Wiggins.

00:37:04.320 --> 00:37:05.320
Come in, Cathy.

00:37:05.320 --> 00:37:24.030
It's no longer possible for me to hide from others.

00:37:24.030 --> 00:37:25.470
I've come to warn you.

00:37:25.470 --> 00:37:26.320
I know.

00:37:26.320 --> 00:37:28.800
The constable's already sent two men down here.

00:37:30.190 --> 00:37:34.190
Why aren't you afraid of me?

00:37:34.190 --> 00:37:37.040
Friends, Willem.

00:37:37.040 --> 00:37:39.250
You've always been kind to me.

00:37:39.250 --> 00:37:45.380
Are you still not afraid of me?

00:37:45.380 --> 00:37:57.170
I saw Willem. What happened to him?

00:37:57.170 --> 00:38:00.000
What terrible thing have you done? You ruined it!

00:38:21.980 --> 00:38:27.310
Where are you going?

00:38:27.310 --> 00:38:30.000
The utterly destroyed example

00:38:30.030 --> 00:38:41.620
must be made. You're wrong. The human race has a gift, professor, a gift that sets it above all

00:38:41.620 --> 00:38:49.120
the other creatures that are bound upon this planet, the gift of thought, of reasoning,

00:38:49.120 --> 00:38:59.160
of understanding, the highly developed brain. But the human race has ceased to develop,

00:39:00.120 --> 00:39:03.340
It struggles for petty comfort and false security.

00:39:03.420 --> 00:39:04.930
There is no time for thought.

00:39:06.680 --> 00:39:11.460
Soon there will be no time for reasoning and man will lose sight of the truth.

00:39:11.460 --> 00:39:17.540
The whole town must be utterly destroyed.

00:39:17.600 --> 00:39:19.780
An example must be made.

00:39:20.250 --> 00:39:25.160
Stand back.

00:40:05.950 --> 00:40:18.850
All that is left of my Willem is his hatred of the town.

00:40:52.650 --> 00:40:55.540
Your ignorance makes me ill and angry.

00:41:03.960 --> 00:41:13.530
Your savageness must end.

00:41:50.160 --> 00:41:51.240
- What happened?

00:41:51.240 --> 00:41:53.030
- He was just like a blinding light.

00:41:53.030 --> 00:41:56.500
Then all of a sudden, but he didn't hurt me,

00:41:56.500 --> 00:41:59.190
just as if he suddenly changed his mind.

00:42:00.160 --> 00:42:08.890
- Don't be afraid. I came back because I knew you were here. - What have you done?

00:42:08.890 --> 00:42:30.000
- I was going to destroy everyone. - And suddenly I evolved beyond hatred or revenge or even the desire for power.

00:42:31.600 --> 00:42:40.490
reaching that stage in the dim future of mankind when the mind will cast off the hamperings of

00:42:40.490 --> 00:43:00.000
the flesh become all thought no matter vortex pure intelligence space it is the goal

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:08.980
of evolution man's final destiny is to become what he imagined in the beginning when he first

00:43:08.980 --> 00:43:16.360
learned the idea of the angel but that is far ahead and i'm impatient to go the whole way

00:43:16.360 --> 00:43:27.350
but that is why i need your help why help you're the only one i can trust will you help me to go

00:43:27.350 --> 00:43:27.770
forward

00:43:30.830 --> 00:43:32.410
I shall return to that chamber.

00:43:33.910 --> 00:43:37.190
You must turn this style to its furthest limit.

00:43:37.890 --> 00:43:39.510
All the way into the future.

00:43:41.640 --> 00:43:43.280
To infinity.

00:43:44.460 --> 00:43:46.030
You understand?

00:43:54.510 --> 00:43:56.030
You're crying.

00:43:56.820 --> 00:43:58.220
You mustn't go any further.

00:43:58.810 --> 00:43:59.530
Come back.

00:44:00.830 --> 00:44:01.760
where you were?

00:44:01.760 --> 00:44:08.970
Kathy, it was you who took me out of the blackness.

00:44:08.970 --> 00:44:12.970
It was you who helped me to come this far, to make it possible.

00:44:12.970 --> 00:44:25.100
Won't you help me now achieve the ultimate?

00:44:25.100 --> 00:44:29.760
Come, Kathy.

00:44:33.070 --> 00:44:59.800
We haven't much time to the chamber, push this.

00:45:00.250 --> 00:45:06.910
to the word forward, all the way, do you understand?

00:45:06.910 --> 00:45:16.600
Not backward, that's into the past.

00:45:16.600 --> 00:45:18.310
That operates the door.

00:45:50.410 --> 00:45:54.100
must I break the last barrier between the flesh and the spirit.

00:46:05.790 --> 00:46:07.110
Goodbye, Kathy.

00:49:37.040 --> 00:49:51.050
I brought him back, I think he's glad he touched me.

00:49:51.050 --> 00:50:00.000
Experiment too soon, too swift, and yet may we not still hope to discover a method by which within

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:07.880
One generation, the whole human race could be rendered intelligent, beyond hatred or revenge or the desire for power.

00:50:09.040 --> 00:50:12.880
Is that not, after all, the ultimate goal of evolution?

00:50:15.280 --> 00:50:20.690
We now return control of your television set to you until next week at this same time,

00:50:20.690 --> 00:50:25.760
when the control voice will take you to The Outer Limits.
